        "input": {
          "instructions": "Clear, measured, and instructor-ready.",
          "text": "The first recovery task is not to defend the system. It is to lower uncertainty. Listen without interrupting, acknowledge the specific impact, clarify what the guest needs now, and make ownership visible. A useful response might be: 'You expected to settle in immediately, and we have delayed your rest. I will stay with this until we have a room or an alternative. ' That sentence does not promise an impossible outcome. It demonstrates understanding and accountability. Diagnosis then separates the immediate need—safe accommodation—from secondary needs such as luggage, transportation, privacy, or schedule changes."
        },
