        "input": {
          "instructions": "Clear, measured, and instructor-ready.",
          "text": "A good remedy is fast, relevant, and proportionate. A generic coupon may be cheap but irrelevant to a guest who needs sleep. An extravagant concession may solve the complaint but create inconsistency and unfairness. The recovery package should address both outcome and process: secure a comparable room, minimize additional effort, explain the next steps, and provide an appropriate acknowledgment of the inconvenience. Employees need authority boundaries so they can act without repeatedly escalating. Consistency matters, but consistency means applying clear principles—not giving every guest the identical gesture regardless of impact."
        },
